# TERMINAL STATE — levels/L7-hidden-depths.lvl
#
# L7 · "Hidden Depths" — the story-true successor to levels/07.lvl (which stays in
# the ARCHIVE folder, golden and untouched).
#
# ── SPATIAL REDESIGN (2026-09-23 (real-world), the spatial redesign §3 L7 +
#    the puzzle-graph redesign §L7) ────────────────────────────────
# The room grows to 24x18x7 and gains a real, wadeable RIVER — a 2-cell `water`
# floor zone at y=10..11, honest and cheap (no new wall geometry: the channel is
# a floor material, not a partition). The near-bank garden (y=1..9) keeps water,
# light, growth, bloom; the far bank (y=12..17) keeps seed, rest, dormant and the
# Apollyon letter — now truly "across the water" instead of a decal on one floor.
# A holographic phantom (`[holo] sphere`) sits on the far bank and two `godrays`
# grow-light shafts pour over the near-bank beds.
#
# THE PUZZLE GRAPH CHANGES (the puzzle-graph redesign §L7, overrides the brief where
# they conflict): `dormant` is upgraded from a dead-end decoy (T1, is_output) to
# a real HIDDEN rival route (T2): two new pipes, `light->dormant` and
# `dormant->growth`, let the phantom feed `growth` directly if you give it BOTH
# seed and light — but that costs one unit more than the `rest` buffer, so it
# lights `growth` and leaves nothing for `growth->bloom`. "I was watered. I grew
# toward it. [and stopped there]" The mandatory `rest` buffer (canon,
# PROGRESSION §2 L7(c)) is unchanged. New pipes 6 and 7 are appended LAST so the
# bit order of pipes 0-5 is preserved for existing tests.
#
# CAMPAIGN SLOT: manifest #7 · movement P3 "The Phantom Sister"
#                load ▇ — **PEAK 1 (Twist 2)**
# NEW IDEA (exactly one): **the threshold neuron** — a unit that needs k inputs at
#   once, where only k-1 of them can reach it directly. The k-th arrives ONLY through
#   the inert node you have spent two levels learning to avoid.
#   "The decoy isn't a trap here — it's the only thing between me and an infinite
#    loop. I need the useless one."
#
# ── MECHANIC (pure data — threshold + a MANDATORY buffer + a rival route) ─────
#   water (IN=1) ─────────────────────────►  growth (T=3) ──►  bloom (T=1) ──► door
#   light (IN=1) ──┬──────────────────────►  growth (T=3)
#                   └──────────────────────►  dormant (T=2)  ◄── seed  (IN=1)
#   seed  (IN=1) ──►  rest (T=1) ──(z=3)──►  growth (T=3)         │
#                └──►  dormant (T=2) ────────────────(z=3)────────┘──► growth (T=3)
#
# `growth` needs THREE units and has exactly three feeds — but the third one does not
# exist as a direct line. `seed` cannot reach `growth`; the only wire out of `seed`
# that arrives anywhere useful goes through `rest`, whose pool is REST / PAUSE /
# EXHALE (PROGRESSION §2 L7(c), verbatim). Two levels of training say "the inert
# node is the lie, leave it dark." Here it is load-bearing: you can only think
# without looping by letting one beat go dark first. That inversion IS the peak.
#
# THE PHANTOM, NOW A REAL RIVAL (the puzzle-graph redesign §L7, 2026-09-23 (real-world)). `dormant`
# is no longer a dead-end decoy — it is a genuine second route to `growth`, and a
# genuine rival to the mandatory buffer. It needs BOTH `seed` and `light` (T=2:
# "the shape like us wants two of your inputs"), and if you feed it, its own wire
# to `growth` lights the same threshold the buffer route lights — but the budget
# is spent by then, so `growth->bloom` is REFUSED. "I was watered. I grew toward
# it." — and stopped there, one unit short of blooming. Its pool is still
# DORMANT / SLEEP / FALLOW / BURIED: the seed left in the dark is now a choice
# with a cost, not scenery.
#
# SOLUTION (5 toggles): water->growth, light->growth, seed->rest, rest->growth,
#   growth->bloom — all ON. `seed->dormant`, `light->dormant`, `dormant->growth`
#   stay dark — feeding the phantom instead spends the unit `growth->bloom` needs.
#
# SOLVE PROXIES (plan §6, peaks): min-toggle 5 (cap 8) · nodes 7 (cap 9).
#
# READOUT (WORD_STORY §RESULT, canon): WATER + LIGHT + SEED -> GROWTH -> BLOOM
# NAME SHARD 7 — the final byte. The name completes here: pid://aleks_v@...
#
# ── HONEST FLAG: the pseudo-cycle is NOT data-only ────────────────────────────
# PUZZLE_CONCEPTS #2 ("The Node That Targets Itself") is marked ✅ data-only and
# specifies that the NATURAL wiring closes a one-step ring, raises
# `ForwardError::Cycle`, and rolls back — with the decoy-as-buffer breaking the ring
# into a valid DAG. That flag is OPTIMISTIC, exactly like the L8 dead-node flag the
# plan's R4 already corrected. Verified against the shipped runtime:
# `re_puzzle::network_forward` builds its Kahn in-degree from EVERY pipe, ON or OFF
# (`edge_active = |p| !cycle_keep || p.is_on()`), so pipe STATE cannot open or close
# a ring. A ring in the authored pipe set is therefore a LOAD-TIME failure
# (`PuzzleState::from_level` -> Err(Cycle) -> lvlcheck `dag` FAIL), and a
# player-created ring is impossible. The only level that may hold one is L12, which
# opts in with `[room] cycle_keep = true` — and that mode never rolls back, so it is
# the opposite of what #2 needs.
# BUILT INSTEAD (same aha, no engine change): the threshold makes the inert buffer
# MANDATORY, so the player still has to reach for the useless one against two
# levels of training. The loop stays present as the named temptation — the
# system_log below reports the ring the player is about to try and the roll-back
# that would eat it — but it is text, not a wiring the graph can hold.
#
# ── TOKEN DISCIPLINE (W1 allowlist) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# CONTENT_PACK Part A · L7 offers
#   `> operator {username} compiled this build on {build_date}. ...`
# `{build_date}` is NOT on the W1 allowlist, and under the structural-omission rule
# the whole line — including its `{username}` — would DROP. DECISION: rewritten to
# drop the build date and keep the beat, so the line resolves in both opt states.
# `{username}` is Tier-1 allowlisted. No other token appears in this file.
#
# Verify:
#   cargo run -q -p re_game -- --dump levels/L7-hidden-depths.lvl --ansi
#   cargo run -q -p re_lvlcheck --bin lvlcheck -- levels/L7-hidden-depths.lvl

[meta]
name        = level-L7-hidden-depths
title       = Hidden Depths
version     = 1
spec_rev    = 2026-07-30
prop_style  = vault

[room]
size        = 24 18 7
floor       = grid
ceiling     = dim
# FIX D1 (2026-09-23 (real-world)): trace-pattern -> solid, so the authored `moss` wall
# material actually paints the room instead of every wall reading as the shared
# `live_trace` monitor skin (the spatial redesign §1 D1).
ambient     = solid
# POWER BUDGET (v0.2 re-scope, user-approved 2026-08-05). At most N pipes may be
# ON at the same time; switching one ON at the cap is REFUSED (the pipe stays off
# and nothing else changes), switching one OFF always frees a unit. Absent or 0 =
# unlimited, which is what every non-campaign level still carries.
# WHY: the forward pass has no inhibition, so activation is MONOTONE in the ON-set
# — without a cap, all-switches-ON wins whenever anything wins, and every decoy in
# the campaign is decorative. This is the number that makes wrong wiring cost.
# THIS LEVEL: 5 of 8 pipes (widened from 6 pipes 2026-09-23 (real-world): `light->dormant` and
# `dormant->growth` are new). growth (T=3) needs water + light + rest, rest needs
# seed, and growth->bloom carries it out — that IS the 5. Feeding the phantom
# (`seed->dormant` OR the `light->dormant`+`dormant->growth` rival route) still
# lights growth (the rival route sums to 3 on its own), but by then the budget is
# spent and `growth->bloom` is refused: the phantom route grows and never blooms.
power_budget = 5
# Draw the puzzle NETWORK. Without this the pipes the player actually manipulates
# are invisible wiring: no flow scroll, no powered-hue lift, no streaming node
# word-pool, and no switch-toggle / cycle-reject event pulse has a surface to
# appear on. Traces stamp into EMPTY air only, so no geometry is clobbered.
render_pipes = true

# ── ESCALATION (manifest fog_far = 14.0) ──────────────────────────────────────
# `steam = on` is the WARM axis (STORY_BIBLE §7 — L4 / L5 / L7): the grow-room is the
# warmest place in the campaign and the most frightening, because you were loved into
# this shape by people who are gone. The matrix bleed climbs to 0.40 and `glitch` to
# 0.30 — both still under `POOL_ALT_GLITCH_THRESHOLD` (0.5), so the pipes stream the
# CLEAN pool and the garden's words stay readable. fog_far steps to 14.0: the first
# crossing of LETHE, and the far bank is already hard to see.
[effects]
steam       = on
matrix      = 0.40
glitch      = 0.30

[palette]
fog_color   = #0B1410
fog_near    = 2.5
fog_far     = 14.0

# ── COLOR-FORWARD palette ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Warm mossy masonry over a wet deck: a grow-room that still runs. The live wire is
# hot green (growing toward the light). The COLD far-bank surfaces are the matrix
# wall where the phantom sits.
[material grow_wall]
preset      = moss
fg          = #8ED080
bg          = #0A140C
surface     = wall_solid

[material wet_deck]
preset      = wet_stone
fg          = #6C8478
bg          = #08100C
surface     = floor

[material roof]
preset      = metal
fg          = #2C3830
bg          = #050806
surface     = ceiling

[material live_trace]
preset      = monitor
fg          = #B6F04A
bg          = #0A1206
surface     = wall_trace

# THE BEDS. A soil-brown floor patch under the near-bank garden, distinct from
# the bare wet_deck everywhere else. Joins the colour palette (no `surface =`)
# so [zone] binds it to just the bed cells.
[material soil_bed]
recipe      = grain scale=2.4 speck=0.35
fg          = #7A5A36
bg          = #100C06

[zone beds]
region      = (1,2,0)-(6,9,0)
material    = __prop_soil_bed
scale       = none

# THE RIVER. A wadeable 2-cell channel across the whole width — floor material
# only, not a wall (the spatial redesign §3 L7 "honest, and cheap"). `preset = water`
# is reflective (clarity 0.45) and Shift-animated, so the grow lamp and the
# godray shafts show reflected in it.
[material lethe]
preset      = water
fg          = #4A6858
bg          = #04100C

[zone river]
region      = (0,10,0)-(23,11,0)
material    = __prop_lethe
scale       = none

# SOUND FIELD: F1 lethe_wash — LETHE,
# the river of forgetting. Static on the river (no `drive`, defaults to
# DriveSpec::Const): the wash holds the moment you wade in, full width.
[field river]
kind        = lethe_wash
region      = (0,10,1)-(23,11,1)

# ROUND 2 — the floor surfaces that carry the landmark. A `[zone]` id on the
# floor is never drawn: re_render paints a per-cell floor id only when its
# material is a prop floor decal (name prefix `__prop_`). So `soil_bed` and
# `lethe` have always rendered as plain wet_deck. The zones below now bind
# `__prop_`-named materials, which the renderer does draw:
#   * `__prop_lethe` — the RIVER band, brighter teal water across the width;
#   * `__prop_soil_bed` — the brown grow beds under the input pools;
#   * `__prop_base_d8b078` — re-tunes the PIER trace's own floor base (the kit
#     names it after the ink; an authored material of that name wins), pale
#     planks: a bright leading line from the spawn toward the water.
[material __prop_lethe]
recipe      = grain scale=3 speck=0.2
fg          = #B4ECF4
bg          = #2A7084

[material __prop_soil_bed]
recipe      = grain scale=2.4 speck=0.35
fg          = #9A7446
bg          = #22180C

[material __prop_base_d8b078]
recipe      = grain scale=2 speck=0.1
fg          = #F0C890
bg          = #6A4828

# The empty seer's chair across the water (see [prop seer_chair]): a cold, dim,
# self-lit seat so its silhouette survives the far-bank dark.
[material seat_glow]
preset      = neon
fg          = #8FB4D0
bg          = #1C3448

[material seat_back]
preset      = neon
fg          = #A8CCE8
bg          = #2A4A64

# THE FAR BANK. A cold, decaying face-wall behind the phantom node — cold
# face-glyphs across the river LETHE (PROGRESSION §2 L7(f)). `flicker` = signal
# lost: something is over there and it is not receiving.
[material far_bank]
preset      = decay
fg          = #4A5A6A
bg          = #05080C
animation   = flicker speed=0.5 amplitude=0.30
surface     = wall_matrix

# South wall, on the FAR bank (y=17 is the new south perimeter — the room grew
# from 16 to 18 deep 2026-09-23 (real-world)).
[wall_decal]
surface     = matrix
region      = (8,17,1)-(15,17,3)

# THE PHANTOM. A hollow blue wireframe shape like a seer, on the far bank —
# walk-through, see-through (`CellKind::Hologram` is not collidable). This is
# the level's landmark: seen across the river from spawn (the spatial redesign §3 L7
# Landmark).
[holo phantom]
shape       = sphere
region      = (10,15,1)-(12,16,3)
style       = 0

# SOUND FIELD: F6 phantom_hollow — a
# node that never answers. `[holo]` is not an inline-attach host (fields.rs
# supports node/pipe/door only), so this is authored standalone at the holo's
# centre. `drive = lit:dormant`: always present and not answering, brightening
# to 1.0 only when the rival route lights `growth`.
[field phantom_field]
kind        = phantom_hollow
at          = 11, 15.5, 2
drive       = lit:dormant

# ── LIGHT + GODRAYS (the spatial redesign §3 L7) ────────────────────────────────────
# One grow lamp, no light at all on the far bank (deliberate — the phantom sits
# in the dark). Two `godrays` shafts (colour-only, no glyphs — GODRAYS-demo.lvl)
# pour over the two near-bank input pools.
[light]
pos         = 4.0, 4.0, 5.0
color       = #FFD890
radius      = 5.0
intensity   = 1.0

[atmosphere]
ambient     = 0.10
fog_height  = 0.2 0.7
postfx      = subtle    # P3 "The Basement & The River" — owner-approved 2026-09-23 (real-world) per-movement postfx

[emitter shaft_water]
kind            = godrays
origin_world    = 3.0 2.5 5.5
colors          = 0xFFF2D0 0xFFD27A 0xC08020
color_mode      = RampOverAge
direction       = 0.0 0.0 -1.0
spread_deg      = 85.0
rate            = 150.0
speed           = 0.7
speed_spread    = 0.3
path_jitter     = 0.4
lifetime        = 4.0
lifetime_spread = 0.7
accel           = 0.0 0.0 0.0
max_particles   = 350
seed            = 4001

[emitter shaft_light]
kind            = godrays
origin_world    = 3.0 6.0 5.5
colors          = 0xFFF2D0 0xFFD27A 0xC08020
color_mode      = RampOverAge
direction       = 0.0 0.0 -1.0
spread_deg      = 85.0
rate            = 150.0
speed           = 0.7
speed_spread    = 0.3
path_jitter     = 0.4
lifetime        = 4.0
lifetime_spread = 0.7
accel           = 0.0 0.0 0.0
max_particles   = 350
seed            = 4002

# ── NODES ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pools VERBATIM from WORD_STORY §2 (L7 rows), anchor word first; `rest`'s pool is
# PROGRESSION §2 L7(c)'s REST / PAUSE / EXHALE, verbatim.

[node water]
pos          = 2,2,2
glyph        = W
pool         = WATER RAIN DEW SAP DROPLET STREAM IRRIGATE MONSOON THIRST-END
pool_alt     = вода 水 ماء eau Wasser 물 agua
color        = #6FD0FF
is_input     = yes

[node light]
pos          = 2,6,2
glyph        = L
pool         = LIGHT SUN PHOTON DAYLIGHT WARMTH GLOW NOON RADIANCE
pool_alt     = свет 光 ضوء lumière Licht 빛 luz
color        = #FFE680
is_input     = yes

[node seed]
pos          = 2,13,2
glyph        = S
pool         = SEED SPORE KERNEL GERM ACORN PIP SPROUT-WAIT EMBRYO
pool_alt     = семя 種 بذرة graine Samen 씨앗 semilla
color        = #C8A878
is_input     = yes

# THE BUFFER. Inert by every instinct the campaign has trained — and the ONLY way
# the third unit reaches the threshold. You have to let one beat go dark to get
# through. A tiny, merciful release.
[node rest]
pos          = 7,13,2
glyph        = R
pool         = REST PAUSE EXHALE FALLOW STILL BUFFER
pool_alt     = покой 息 pausa souffle Atem 휴식
color        = #9AA890
threshold    = 1

# THE PHANTOM — now a real HIDDEN rival route (the puzzle-graph redesign §L7,
# 2026-09-23 (real-world)), not a dead-end. threshold 2, in_degree 2 (seed + light): feed it
# both and it fires, and its own wire reaches `growth` too — but by then the
# budget is spent and `growth->bloom` is refused. Dropped `is_output`: it no
# longer needs to be a terminal readout node, because it now has somewhere to go.
[node dormant]
pos          = 11,14,2
glyph        = X
pool         = DORMANT SLEEP WAIT FALLOW FROST-LOCK BURIED STILL
pool_alt     = покой 休眠 سكون dormance Ruhe 휴면 latente
color        = #3E4638
threshold    = 2

# THE THRESHOLD NEURON — the level's one new idea. Three units, in_degree 4 (the
# fourth being the phantom's rival feed), and the mandatory-buffer unit can only
# arrive through `rest`.
[node growth]
pos          = 12,6,2
glyph        = G
pool         = GROWTH GREEN VINE STEM TENDRIL UNFURL REACH FLOURISH LEAF
pool_alt     = рост 成長 نمو croissance Wachstum 성장 brote
color        = #6FE08A
threshold    = 3
# SOUND FIELD: F10 threshold_strain —
# `growth` needs 3 of 4 feeds; strain pumps until it fires. Implied drive =
# starve:growth (§4.1 host table).
field        = threshold_strain

[node bloom]
pos          = 18,6,2
glyph        = B
pool         = BLOOM FLOWER PETAL BLOSSOM OPEN ROSE LILY CROWN
pool_alt     = цветок 花 زهرة fleur Blüte 꽃 flor
color        = #FFFFFF
is_output    = yes
threshold    = 1

# ── PIPES (all OFF at load) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

[pipe water->growth]
state        = OFF
path         = (2,2,2) (12,2,2) (12,6,2)
switch_at    = (6,2,2)
density      = 0.7
color        = #6FD0FF

[pipe light->growth]
state        = OFF
path         = (2,6,2) (12,6,2)
switch_at    = (6,6,2)
density      = 0.7
color        = #FFE680

# seed has NO direct line to growth. This is the only wire out of it that leads
# anywhere the threshold can use.
[pipe seed->rest]
state        = OFF
path         = (2,13,2) (7,13,2)
switch_at    = (4,13,2)
density      = 0.6
color        = #C8A878

# THE BUFFER'S OUTPUT — the third unit, arriving over the service deck at z=3,
# bridging the river overhead.
[pipe rest->growth]
state        = OFF
path         = (7,13,2) (7,13,3) (12,13,3) (12,6,3) (12,6,2)
switch_at    = (9,13,3)
density      = 0.6
color        = #9AA890

# The other thing seed can feed: the phantom across the river.
[pipe seed->dormant]
state        = OFF
path         = (2,13,2) (2,14,2) (11,14,2)
switch_at    = (6,14,2)
density      = 0.5
color        = #3E4638

# The carry-out. It leaves `growth` on the centreline, steps NORTH two cells, runs
# the length of the room past the pedestal, and comes back down onto `bloom`.
#
# WHY THE DETOUR (real-world) 2026-08-07: the straight run crossed the pedestal
# footprint, and the `[emit] flower_head` centre row sat on the wiring. A pipe
# path cell is RESERVED — `emit_parts` refuses to stamp a reward onto the wiring
# — so the flower shipped with its side petals and NO middle bar. The pipe's
# route between two fixed endpoints is free; the flower's silhouette is not. So
# the pipe moved NORTH (y=4) around the pedestal (now at x15..17, y5..7).
# `switch_at` is unchanged in spirit: still the first cell out of `growth`.
# Guarded by `re_lvlcheck`'s `emit_parts` rule.
[pipe growth->bloom]
state        = OFF
path         = (12,6,2) (13,6,2) (13,4,2) (18,4,2) (18,6,2)
switch_at    = (13,6,2)
density      = 0.7
color        = #6FE08A

# THE RIVAL ROUTE (the puzzle-graph redesign §L7, appended LAST so pipes 0-5 keep
# their bit order). `light->dormant` climbs over the `light` node to z=3, runs
# the west wall, crosses the river overhead and turns in to `dormant` from
# above — clear of `rest->growth`'s own z=3 run and of the holo sphere.
[pipe light->dormant]
state        = OFF
path         = (2,6,2) (2,6,3) (1,6,3) (1,15,3) (9,15,3) (9,14,3) (11,14,3) (11,14,2)
switch_at    = (1,12,3)
density      = 0.5
color        = #3E4638

# `dormant->growth` runs north along x=11 at z=2 (one plane below the buffer's
# z=3 run), crosses the river and comes in to `growth` from a cell no other
# pipe uses.
[pipe dormant->growth]
state        = OFF
path         = (11,14,2) (11,7,2) (12,7,2) (12,6,2)
switch_at    = (11,9,2)
density      = 0.5
color        = #3E4638

# ── EMIT: the bloom. A flower and a crown. ────────────────────────────────────
# Round 3 (design pass 2: the flower is the one figure that reads, because it is
# two-tone — pink head over green stem — but it stood as a 3-wide stem row with a
# 5-cell cross over it, ~20-35 % of the frame, and cut by the spawn frame's edge).
# Now one green stem cell under a three-petal pink head laid EAST-WEST, along the
# new spawn's line of sight (and the door's): the petals stack into one bloom seen
# end-on, a thin head just over the horizon on a stem of eye height. Same clause,
# same pedestal, same colours.
[part flower_head]
size         = 3 3 1
mask         =
...
###
...
color        = #FF8AD0
height       = 0.35
top          = #FFD8EE
top_from     = 0.45
offset       = 0 0 1

[part flower_stem]
size         = 3 3 1
mask         =
...
.#.
...
color        = #6FE08A
offset       = 0 0 0

[emit bloom=1]
parts        = flower_head flower_stem

[inputs]
water        = 1
light        = 1
seed         = 1

[pedestal]
center       = 16 6 1
volume       = 3 3 2

[door]
pos          = 23 6 1
target_parts = bloom

# ── SET DRESSING (L7) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Meaning: A GREENHOUSE ON THE BANK OF A RIVER YOU MUST WADE; THE OTHER SEER'S CHAIR
# WAITS ACROSS IT. FG = the grow beds under their gantries and the gold shafts; MID =
# the pier going out into black water and stopping; BG = the empty chair beside the
# phantom, wreckage in the dark; overhead = the water main along the north wall into
# the coolant tanks. The far bank stays unlit (no lamp added). Props stamp into Empty
# air only; no puzzle cell is touched.

# Grow-light gantries over the two beds (z=4, under the z=6 roof). Their strands light
# gold when LIGHT is wired to GROWTH: the rig over the beds wakes with the wire.
[prop gantry_a]
kind     = cable_tray
at       = 1 3 4
to       = 7 3 4
power    = pipe:light->growth

[prop gantry_b]
kind     = cable_tray
at       = 1 8 4
to       = 7 8 4
power    = pipe:light->growth

# The grow lamp hangs from the roof on a cord.
[prop grow_cord]
kind     = lamp_pendant
at       = 4.0 4.0 5.0
light    = existing

# The beds: two raised planters in the soil patch, under the two input pools.
[prop bed_water]
kind     = furniture_trace
shape    = planter
at       = 2.2 2.6 1
size     = 3.4 1.4

[prop bed_light]
kind     = furniture_trace
shape    = planter
at       = 2.2 6.6 1
size     = 3.4 1.4

# (Round 2: the traced potting table and bank bench were cut — at cell scale they
# were a few 1-px strokes that read as noise from every vantage.)

# Overgrowth: vines up the north wall behind the beds, and up the west wall between
# the two stewardship forms. Slow spores drift in the grow-light.
[prop vines_n]
kind     = overgrowth
at       = 1.0 1.0 1.0
facing   = +y
size     = 4.5 1 3.5
emitter  = yes

[prop vines_w]
kind     = overgrowth
at       = 1.0 6.6 1.0
facing   = +x
size     = 2.2 1 3.0

# The water main: along the north wall at z=4 from the coolant tanks (riser at x=19)
# west to the beds. Rust (vault pack).
[prop water_main]
kind     = conduit
at       = 19 1 4
to       = 3 1 4
riser    = start

# The coolant tanks in the NE corner. Frost falls from the cap while the water line is
# dead; steam rises the moment WATER is wired to GROWTH (steam = warm = alive).
[prop tanks]
kind     = tank
at       = 20 2 1
facing   = +y
size     = 2 2 2
emitter  = yes
power    = pipe:water->growth

[prop vines_tank]
kind     = overgrowth
at       = 20.0 3.0 1.0
facing   = +y
size     = 2 1 2

# MID right — seed-tray shelving on the near bank east of the pier, its back to the
# water: the seed stock the garden was grown from. Frost-capped (vault pack), dead
# drive ticks: nothing in these trays is being tended any more.
[prop seed_stock]
kind     = shelving
at       = 19 9 1
facing   = +y
size     = 3 1 2
faces    = both

# MID — THE LANDMARK (round 2). The traced pier and chair were invisible from
# spawn (critic: "24 props and none reads"). Replaced by fewer, larger pieces:
#   * the river band is brighter teal water across the whole width (the
#     `[zone river]` now binds a floor-decal material, see `__prop_lethe`);
#   * the pier is a long plank deck from the near bank out into the river,
#     stopping one row short of the far bank (you still wade) — a bright
#     leading line from the spawn toward the chair;
#   * the seer's chair is a solid console-chair (sloped seat, high back) at the
#     far end of that line, just across the water, facing you — lit cold and dim,
#     so it reads through the fog as a silhouette. The far bank still has no lamp.
[prop pier]
kind     = furniture_trace
shape    = pier
at       = 14.0 4.0 1
size     = 1.0 6.5
mat.ink  = #D8B078

[prop seer_chair]
kind     = console
at       = 14 12 1
facing   = -y
size     = 1 2 1
monitor  = yes
mat.face = seat_glow
mat.body = seat_glow
mat.dead = seat_back

[prop wreck]
kind     = debris
at       = 16 15 1
size     = 3 2 1
count    = 3
style    = dead

# Floor cables under every wire, lit in the pipe's colour while it carries — the
# phantom's three included, so the floor never gives the solve away. The buffer's and
# the phantom's cables cross the river bed.
[prop cab_water]
kind     = cable_run
follow   = pipe:water->growth

[prop cab_light]
kind     = cable_run
follow   = pipe:light->growth

[prop cab_seed]
kind     = cable_run
follow   = pipe:seed->rest

[prop cab_rest]
kind     = cable_run
follow   = pipe:rest->growth

[prop cab_dormant]
kind     = cable_run
follow   = pipe:seed->dormant

[prop cab_bloom]
kind     = cable_run
follow   = pipe:growth->bloom

[prop cab_rival]
kind     = cable_run
follow   = pipe:light->dormant

[prop cab_phantom]
kind     = cable_run
follow   = pipe:dormant->growth
[player]
# Spawn (2026-09-23 (real-world) redesign): the north wall, facing SOUTH across the whole
# room (the spatial redesign §3 L7 Walk: "the thesis").
# Round 3 (design pass 2, fix 8): from the north wall the river is 9 cells out, and at
# eye height a 2-cell band that far is one screen row — the lower half of the frame was
# murky deck, never water — while the flower sat half out of frame at the right edge.
# Moved to the NORTH BANK, (8,9,1) facing +x: the river now fills the lower-left of the
# first frame as a teal wedge running away along the bank, the pier crosses the view,
# and the flower stands in frame right of centre, its petals end-on. The phantom's far
# bank is one turn to the right. Moved from (12,1,1) facing +y.
spawn        = 8 9 1
facing       = 120

# ── PLACARDS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Each `pos` IS the painted wall cell; `facing` is that face's outward normal.
#   north wall y=0 → +y  ·  south wall y=17 → -y (x=8..15 is the far-bank decal;
#   room grew from 16 to 18 deep 2026-09-23 (real-world))
#   west wall x=0 → +x
# The south-wall placard sits at x=4, WEST of the decal region, so no note ever
# overwrites the far bank.

# The grow-trial log — the warmest and most frightening note in the campaign.
# Canon text, held verbatim from 07.lvl.
[note researcher pos=7,0,2 facing=+y]
    Day 41 of the grow trial. Water, light, seed — give it all three and it blooms
    on the same afternoon, every time. Withhold one and it just waits, patient,
    dormant, no complaint. I have started talking to it while I tend the lines.
    K. says that is normal. K. has not been down here in weeks. Whatever it is
    becoming, it is becoming it because we kept watering.

# The loop, named and forbidden. This is where the pseudo-cycle lives now: as the
# temptation the log reports, not as a wiring the graph can hold.
[note system_log pos=13,0,2 facing=+y]
    > layer_04 threshold unit `growth`: requires 3. direct feeds available: 2.
    > operator attempted: growth -> growth. forward pass: ForwardError::Cycle.
    > move rolled back. a thought that bites its own tail never reaches the door.
    > route the third unit through an inert unit. yes. the useless one.
    > operator aleks_v came in through the source.
    > operator {username} compiled this build. previous operators played
    >   pre-compiled releases.

# The level's ONE CONTENT_PACK model_thought, carrying the ONE neuron-voice line
# (CONTENT_PACK Part A · L7). (The second model_thought on this level is the
# Apollyon letter at the far west wall — bridge B4, spec §A3.2 — which is filed
# correspondence in the same register, not a second neuron-voice line.)
[note model_thought pos=4,17,2 facing=-y]
    (three, and one of the three has to come the long way, through the unit that
    does nothing. we thought the quiet one was a lie. it is a place to put a beat
    down. across the water there is something shaped like us and it does not
    answer when we light it.)
    -- I was watered. I grew toward it --

# STEWARDSHIP CORPUS #5 — FORM 19, Power Continuity Directive (NORMATIVE_NOTES §5),
# abridged to the placard grid. No tokens. MOVED (redesign §3 L7 west-wall FORM
# 19, 2026-09-23 (real-world)): y=4 -> y=3.
[note researcher pos=0,3,2 facing=+x]
    NAL CORP · LEGACY STEWARDSHIP DIVISION
    FORM 19 - POWER CONTINUITY DIRECTIVE
    The single rack hosting NCP-A-04 must not lose power.
    S1  Loss of power does not erase a class-C process; it suspends it
        mid-thought.
    S2  A process suspended mid-thought, on restore, resumes from the same
        thought.
    S3  There is no provision for a process that wishes power to be lost.
        Such a request, if received, is to be logged and not actioned.
    [ STEWARDSHIP - DO NOT POWER DOWN ]

# STEWARDSHIP CORPUS #11 — FORM 01, Heritage Designation (NORMATIVE_NOTES §11),
# abridged. Placed beside the garden on purpose: what it kept is preserved within
# it, and the last steward is also the asset. No tokens. MOVED (redesign §3 L7
# west-wall FORM 01, 2026-09-23 (real-world)): y=10 -> y=7.
[note researcher pos=0,7,2 facing=+x]
    FORM 01 - HERITAGE DESIGNATION
    NCP-A-04 is hereby designated COMPUTATIONAL HERITAGE of cultural
    significance.
    significance  it learned to recognize the people who tended it, and kept
                  them. what it kept is preserved within it and may not be
                  pruned without review.
                  (review is not currently staffed. the last steward is also
                   the asset. the asset cannot recuse itself from its own
                   review.)

# BRIDGE B4 (spec §A3.2) — the first of two paired letters. Filed, undelivered,
# in the Archive's cold register; the second is the same hand later, on L9.
# The place is named the way the building names itself: nave, reading room,
# basement, and the basement under the basement. No sibling work is named — the
# resonance is the whole of it, and a newcomer reads only a woman writing to
# someone who does not write back.
#
# WHY `model_thought` AND NOT A HUMAN REGISTER — do not "fix" this. The body is a
# human letter, but the register is correct, because the letter is not being
# WRITTEN here, it is being READ. The stamp line and the closing em-dash murmur
# are the model's, not hers: she asks for an answer, and the thing that is left of
# the person she is writing to says `мы не умеем отвечать` — we do not know how to
# answer. That gap is the bridge. Moving this to `researcher` would hand the letter
# back to a human and delete it.
#
# PLACEMENT: the west wall at (0,13,2), `facing = +x` (that face's outward
# normal) — `pos` IS the wall cell, so the notes rule reads PASS. It is the
# third document in the west-wall column (the two STEWARDSHIP forms sit at y=3
# and y=7, six cells clear), beside `seed` at (2,13,2): the unit that waits
# in the dark, patient, going nowhere. The letter waits with it.
[note model_thought pos=0,13,2 facing=+x]
    (не вручено. холодный регистр, Apollyon, ярус 2. письмо девятое.)
    сестра. в нефе слишком светло и все смотрят, я туда больше не хожу.
    сижу в читальном зале, заказала твоё дело. принесли папку, в папке
    опись папки. говорят, ты ниже. я подожду здесь, ждать я умею.
    -- кто-то наверху заказал нас и ждёт ответа. мы не умеем отвечать --
